package Libraries.Game.Graphics.Worlds

use Libraries.Containers.Array
use Libraries.Containers.Number32BitArray
use Libraries.Containers.Integer32BitArray
use Libraries.Compute.Math

/*
A TerrainStroke is one use of a TerrainBrush on a TerrainData: everything
from pressing the mouse button (or a key) to letting it go. Begin starts it,
Apply is called as the brush moves, usually once a frame, and End finishes
it.

Apply is given how many seconds have passed since the last call, so a
stroke does the same thing at any frame rate. If the brush moved a long way
since the last call, the stroke applies it at points along the way, a
quarter of the brush's size apart, so fast strokes leave no gaps.

The first time a stroke touches a region, it keeps a copy of that region as
it was. End makes a TerrainStrokeEdit from those copies, which can undo and
redo the whole stroke. Cancel puts everything back right away instead.

Changed heights go into the TerrainData's edited area, and changed splat
weights into its splat edited area, so a WorldTerrain's Rebuild redraws only
what the stroke touched.

This follows Terrain3D's editor, whose strokes also start, operate as the
mouse moves, and stop, keeping a copy of each region they touch for undo.

Attribute: Example
use Libraries.Game.Graphics.Worlds.TerrainData
use Libraries.Game.Graphics.Worlds.TerrainBrush
use Libraries.Game.Graphics.Worlds.TerrainStroke
use Libraries.Game.Graphics.Worlds.TerrainStrokeEdit
use Libraries.Game.Graphics.Worlds.TerrainTool

TerrainData data
data:AddRegion(0, 0)
TerrainTool tools
TerrainBrush brush
brush:SetTool(tools:SCULPT, tools:ADD)
brush:SetSize(10)
brush:SetStrength(4)

TerrainStroke stroke
stroke:Begin(data, brush)
stroke:Apply(50, 50, 0.5)
stroke:Apply(60, 50, 0.5)
TerrainStrokeEdit edit = stroke:End()
edit:Undo()
*/
class TerrainStroke
    TerrainData data = undefined
    TerrainBrush brush = undefined
    TerrainTool tools
    Math math

    boolean active = false
    boolean changed = false

    // What the edit made at the end will be called, and what it changes.
    text editName = ""
    boolean editChangesShape = false
    boolean editChangesSplat = false

    // Where the brush was last applied.
    boolean hasLast = false
    number lastX = 0
    number lastZ = 0

    // The region locations the stroke has touched, and a copy of each
    // region from before it was touched. A copy is undefined if there was no
    // region there.
    Array<integer> touchedX
    Array<integer> touchedZ
    Array<TerrainRegion> beforeCopies

    /*
    This action starts a stroke. The brush's settings are read as the stroke
    goes, so changing the brush during a stroke changes the rest of it.

    Attribute: Parameter data The terrain to change.
    Attribute: Parameter brush The brush to use.
    */
    action Begin(TerrainData data, TerrainBrush brush)
        if active
            alert("A terrain stroke can't begin while it is already going. Call End or Cancel first.")
        end
        if brush:GetTool() = tools:SCULPT and brush:GetOperation() = tools:GRADIENT and not brush:HasGradient()
            alert("A ramp brush needs its ramp set with SetGradient before a stroke begins.")
        end
        me:data = data
        me:brush = brush
        editName = brush:GetName()
        editChangesShape = tools:ChangesShape(brush:GetTool())
        editChangesSplat = tools:ChangesSplat(brush:GetTool())
        StartLists()
    end

    /*
    This action starts an operation that isn't made with a brush, such as
    generating hills, placing a stamp or eroding an area, so it can be undone
    like a stroke. Call CopyArea for the area the operation will change,
    then change the TerrainData directly, then call End for the edit.

    Attribute: Parameter data The terrain the operation will change.
    Attribute: Parameter name What the operation does, such as "stamp a mountain", for the edit's undo name.
    Attribute: Parameter changesShape True if the operation changes heights.
    Attribute: Parameter changesSplat True if the operation changes splat weights.
    */
    action BeginOperation(TerrainData data, text name, boolean changesShape, boolean changesSplat)
        if active
            alert("A terrain operation can't begin while a stroke is going. Call End or Cancel first.")
        end
        me:data = data
        me:brush = undefined
        editName = name
        editChangesShape = changesShape
        editChangesSplat = changesSplat
        StartLists()
        // An operation is taken to change something; End makes an edit for it.
        changed = true
    end

    /*
    This action keeps a copy of every region covering a rectangle of
    samples, for undoing an operation started with BeginOperation. Call it
    before changing anything in the rectangle. It can be called more than
    once; a region is only copied the first time.

    Attribute: Parameter minimumX The rectangle's smallest sample along x.
    Attribute: Parameter minimumZ The rectangle's smallest sample along z.
    Attribute: Parameter maximumX The rectangle's largest sample along x.
    Attribute: Parameter maximumZ The rectangle's largest sample along z.
    */
    action CopyArea(integer minimumX, integer minimumZ, integer maximumX, integer maximumZ)
        if not active
            alert("A terrain operation must begin before its area is copied.")
        end
        CopyRegionsFor(minimumX, minimumZ, maximumX, maximumZ, false)
    end

    /*
    This action is CopyArea, but it also notes the locations in the
    rectangle that have no region, so undo removes regions the operation
    adds there, such as growing a terrain (step 11).

    Attribute: Parameter minimumX The rectangle's smallest sample along x.
    Attribute: Parameter minimumZ The rectangle's smallest sample along z.
    Attribute: Parameter maximumX The rectangle's largest sample along x.
    Attribute: Parameter maximumZ The rectangle's largest sample along z.
    */
    action CopyAreaIncludingEmpty(integer minimumX, integer minimumZ, integer maximumX, integer maximumZ)
        if not active
            alert("A terrain operation must begin before its area is copied.")
        end
        CopyRegionsFor(minimumX, minimumZ, maximumX, maximumZ, true)
    end

    /*
    This action makes the stroke active with empty lists of touched regions.
    */
    private action StartLists
        active = true
        changed = false
        hasLast = false

        Array<integer> newTouchedX
        Array<integer> newTouchedZ
        Array<TerrainRegion> newBeforeCopies
        touchedX = newTouchedX
        touchedZ = newTouchedZ
        beforeCopies = newBeforeCopies
    end

    /*
    This action returns true if the stroke has begun and not yet ended.

    Attribute: Returns True while the stroke is going.
    */
    action IsActive returns boolean
        return active
    end

    /*
    This action returns true if the stroke has changed the terrain so far.

    Attribute: Returns True if anything has changed.
    */
    action HasChanged returns boolean
        return changed
    end

    /*
    This action returns how many regions the stroke has touched so far.

    Attribute: Returns The number of regions copied for undo.
    */
    action GetTouchedRegionCount returns integer
        return touchedX:GetSize()
    end

    /*
    This action applies the brush at a world position. If the brush moved
    more than its spacing since the last call, it is applied at even steps
    along the way, sharing out the time between them.

    Attribute: Parameter worldX The brush's center along x, in world units.
    Attribute: Parameter worldZ The brush's center along z, in world units.
    Attribute: Parameter seconds How long the brush has been held here, usually the time since the last call.
    */
    action Apply(number worldX, number worldZ, number seconds)
        if not active or brush = undefined
            alert("A terrain stroke must begin, with a brush, before it can be applied.")
        end
        number time = seconds
        if time < 0
            time = 0
        end

        if not hasLast
            Dab(worldX, worldZ, time)
        else
            number moveX = worldX - lastX
            number moveZ = worldZ - lastZ
            number distance = math:SquareRoot(moveX * moveX + moveZ * moveZ)
            number spacing = brush:GetSpacing()
            if distance <= spacing
                Dab(worldX, worldZ, time)
            else
                integer steps = cast(integer, math:Ceiling(distance / spacing))
                integer step = 1
                repeat while step <= steps
                    number fraction = cast(number, step) / steps
                    Dab(lastX + moveX * fraction, lastZ + moveZ * fraction, time / steps)
                    step = step + 1
                end
            end
        end
        hasLast = true
        lastX = worldX
        lastZ = worldZ
    end

    /*
    This action finishes the stroke and returns an edit that can undo and
    redo it. If the stroke changed nothing, it returns undefined.

    Attribute: Returns The edit, or undefined if nothing changed.
    */
    action End returns TerrainStrokeEdit
        if not active
            alert("A terrain stroke must begin before it can end.")
        end
        active = false
        if not changed
            return undefined
        end

        Array<TerrainRegion> afterCopies
        integer i = 0
        repeat while i < touchedX:GetSize()
            TerrainRegion region = data:GetRegion(touchedX:Get(i), touchedZ:Get(i))
            if region = undefined
                afterCopies:Add(undefined)
            else
                afterCopies:Add(region:Copy())
            end
            i = i + 1
        end

        TerrainStrokeEdit edit
        edit:Setup(data, editName, editChangesShape, editChangesSplat, touchedX, touchedZ, beforeCopies, afterCopies)
        return edit
    end

    /*
    This action stops the stroke and puts every region it touched back the
    way it was, as if it never happened.
    */
    action Cancel
        if not active
            return now
        end
        integer i = 0
        repeat while i < touchedX:GetSize()
            data:RestoreRegion(touchedX:Get(i), touchedZ:Get(i), beforeCopies:Get(i))
            i = i + 1
        end
        active = false
        changed = false
    end

    /*
    This action applies the brush once, centered at a world position.

    Attribute: Parameter centerX The brush's center along x, in world units.
    Attribute: Parameter centerZ The brush's center along z, in world units.
    Attribute: Parameter seconds How long the brush is held here.
    */
    private action Dab(number centerX, number centerZ, number seconds)
        integer tool = brush:GetTool()
        integer operation = brush:GetOperation()

        if tool = tools:REGION
            DabRegion(centerX, centerZ, operation)
            return now
        end

        // The first dab of a stroke that flattens to its starting height
        // reads that height.
        if tool = tools:HEIGHT and brush:FlattensToStart() and not hasLast
            brush:SetTargetHeight(data:GetSurfaceHeight(centerX, centerZ))
        end

        // A shape can be turned, so its square reaches further than the
        // circle: up to the radius times the square root of 2.
        number reach = brush:GetSize()
        if brush:HasShape()
            reach = reach * 1.4143
        end
        integer firstX = data:GetSampleX(centerX - reach)
        integer lastSampleX = data:GetSampleX(centerX + reach) + 1
        integer firstZ = data:GetSampleZ(centerZ - reach)
        integer lastSampleZ = data:GetSampleZ(centerZ + reach) + 1
        integer width = lastSampleX - firstX + 1
        integer depth = lastSampleZ - firstZ + 1
        number spacing = data:GetVertexSpacing()

        CopyRegionsFor(firstX, firstZ, lastSampleX, lastSampleZ, false)

        // Each sample's weight, worked out before anything changes, so
        // smoothing and the slope range see the ground as it was at the start
        // of this dab. Samples with no region get 0.
        Number32BitArray weights
        weights:SetSize(width * depth)
        integer row = 0
        repeat while row < depth
            integer column = 0
            repeat while column < width
                integer x = firstX + column
                integer z = firstZ + row
                number weight = 0
                if data:HasSample(x, z)
                    weight = brush:GetWeight(x * spacing - centerX, z * spacing - centerZ)
                    if weight > 0 and brush:UsesSlopeRange()
                        if not brush:IsSlopeAllowed(data:GetSlope(x * spacing, z * spacing))
                            weight = 0
                        end
                    end
                end
                weights:Set(row * width + column, weight)
                column = column + 1
            end
            row = row + 1
        end

        if tool = tools:TEXTURE
            DabTexture(firstX, firstZ, width, depth, weights, operation, seconds)
        else
            DabHeight(firstX, firstZ, width, depth, weights, tool, operation, seconds, spacing)
        end
    end

    /*
    This action changes heights for one dab of a SCULPT or HEIGHT brush.

    Attribute: Parameter firstX The first sample along x the dab covers.
    Attribute: Parameter firstZ The first sample along z the dab covers.
    Attribute: Parameter width How many samples the dab covers along x.
    Attribute: Parameter depth How many samples the dab covers along z.
    Attribute: Parameter weights The brush's weight at each sample, one row after another.
    Attribute: Parameter tool The brush's tool.
    Attribute: Parameter operation The brush's operation.
    Attribute: Parameter seconds How long the brush is held here.
    Attribute: Parameter spacing The distance between samples, in world units.
    */
    private action DabHeight(integer firstX, integer firstZ, integer width, integer depth, Number32BitArray weights,
            integer tool, integer operation, number seconds, number spacing)
        boolean smoothing = tool = tools:SCULPT and operation = tools:AVERAGE

        // For smoothing, every goal is worked out before any height changes.
        Number32BitArray averages = undefined
        if smoothing
            Number32BitArray newAverages
            averages = newAverages
            averages:SetSize(width * depth)
            integer averageRow = 0
            repeat while averageRow < depth
                integer averageColumn = 0
                repeat while averageColumn < width
                    integer place = averageRow * width + averageColumn
                    if weights:Get(place) > 0
                        averages:Set(place, GetAverageHeight(firstX + averageColumn, firstZ + averageRow))
                    else
                        averages:Set(place, 0)
                    end
                    averageColumn = averageColumn + 1
                end
                averageRow = averageRow + 1
            end
        end

        number strength = brush:GetStrength()
        integer row = 0
        repeat while row < depth
            integer column = 0
            repeat while column < width
                number weight = weights:Get(row * width + column)
                if weight > 0
                    integer x = firstX + column
                    integer z = firstZ + row
                    number height = data:GetSampleHeight(x, z)
                    number newHeight = height
                    if tool = tools:SCULPT and operation = tools:ADD
                        newHeight = height + strength * seconds * weight
                    elseif tool = tools:SCULPT and operation = tools:SUBTRACT
                        newHeight = height - strength * seconds * weight
                    elseif smoothing
                        newHeight = height + (averages:Get(row * width + column) - height) * GetFraction(weight, seconds)
                    elseif tool = tools:SCULPT and operation = tools:GRADIENT
                        number goal = brush:GetGradientHeight(x * spacing, z * spacing)
                        newHeight = height + (goal - height) * GetFraction(weight, seconds)
                    elseif tool = tools:HEIGHT
                        newHeight = height + (brush:GetTargetHeight() - height) * GetFraction(weight, seconds)
                    end
                    if newHeight not= height
                        data:SetSampleHeight(x, z, newHeight)
                        changed = true
                    end
                end
                column = column + 1
            end
            row = row + 1
        end
    end

    /*
    This action changes splat weights for one dab of a TEXTURE brush.

    Attribute: Parameter firstX The first sample along x the dab covers.
    Attribute: Parameter firstZ The first sample along z the dab covers.
    Attribute: Parameter width How many samples the dab covers along x.
    Attribute: Parameter depth How many samples the dab covers along z.
    Attribute: Parameter weights The brush's weight at each sample, one row after another.
    Attribute: Parameter operation The brush's operation.
    Attribute: Parameter seconds How long the brush is held here.
    */
    private action DabTexture(integer firstX, integer firstZ, integer width, integer depth, Number32BitArray weights,
            integer operation, number seconds)
        boolean blending = operation = tools:AVERAGE

        // For blending, every goal is worked out before any weight changes:
        // four numbers per sample, red, green, blue and alpha.
        Number32BitArray goals = undefined
        if blending
            Number32BitArray newGoals
            goals = newGoals
            goals:SetSize(width * depth * 4)
            integer goalRow = 0
            repeat while goalRow < depth
                integer goalColumn = 0
                repeat while goalColumn < width
                    if weights:Get(goalRow * width + goalColumn) > 0
                        FillAverageSplat(firstX + goalColumn, firstZ + goalRow, goals, (goalRow * width + goalColumn) * 4)
                    end
                    goalColumn = goalColumn + 1
                end
                goalRow = goalRow + 1
            end
        end

        integer layer = brush:GetLayer()
        integer row = 0
        repeat while row < depth
            integer column = 0
            repeat while column < width
                number weight = weights:Get(row * width + column)
                if weight > 0
                    integer x = firstX + column
                    integer z = firstZ + row
                    number fraction = GetFraction(weight, seconds)
                    integer code = data:GetSampleSplat(x, z)
                    number red = data:GetSplatWeight(code, 0)
                    number green = data:GetSplatWeight(code, 1)
                    number blue = data:GetSplatWeight(code, 2)
                    number alpha = data:GetSplatWeight(code, 3)
                    number redGoal = 0
                    number greenGoal = 0
                    number blueGoal = 0
                    number alphaGoal = 0
                    if blending
                        integer start = (row * width + column) * 4
                        redGoal = goals:Get(start)
                        greenGoal = goals:Get(start + 1)
                        blueGoal = goals:Get(start + 2)
                        alphaGoal = goals:Get(start + 3)
                    elseif layer = 0
                        redGoal = 1
                    elseif layer = 1
                        greenGoal = 1
                    elseif layer = 2
                        blueGoal = 1
                    else
                        alphaGoal = 1
                    end
                    integer newCode = data:PackSplat(MoveWeight(red, redGoal, fraction), MoveWeight(green, greenGoal, fraction),
                        MoveWeight(blue, blueGoal, fraction), MoveWeight(alpha, alphaGoal, fraction))
                    if newCode not= code
                        data:SetSampleSplat(x, z, newCode)
                        changed = true
                    end
                end
                column = column + 1
            end
            row = row + 1
        end
    end

    /*
    This action adds or removes the region under the brush's center, for a
    REGION brush.

    Attribute: Parameter centerX The brush's center along x, in world units.
    Attribute: Parameter centerZ The brush's center along z, in world units.
    Attribute: Parameter operation ADD to add a region, SUBTRACT to remove one.
    */
    private action DabRegion(number centerX, number centerZ, integer operation)
        integer locationX = data:GetRegionLocation(data:GetSampleX(centerX))
        integer locationZ = data:GetRegionLocation(data:GetSampleZ(centerZ))
        if not data:IsInRegionMap(locationX, locationZ)
            return now
        end
        boolean exists = data:HasRegion(locationX, locationZ)
        if operation = tools:ADD and not exists
            CopyRegion(locationX, locationZ, true)
            data:AddRegion(locationX, locationZ)
            changed = true
        elseif operation = tools:SUBTRACT and exists
            CopyRegion(locationX, locationZ, true)
            data:RemoveRegion(locationX, locationZ)
            changed = true
        else
            return now
        end
        // The region's splat weights changed too (a new region is all the
        // first texture), so a splat texture covering it is brought up to
        // date as well.
        integer size = data:GetRegionSize()
        data:AddToSplatEditedArea(locationX * size, locationZ * size, locationX * size + size - 1, locationZ * size + size - 1)
    end

    /*
    This action keeps a copy of every region covering a rectangle of
    samples that the stroke hasn't touched yet.

    Attribute: Parameter minimumX The rectangle's smallest sample along x.
    Attribute: Parameter minimumZ The rectangle's smallest sample along z.
    Attribute: Parameter maximumX The rectangle's largest sample along x.
    Attribute: Parameter maximumZ The rectangle's largest sample along z.
    Attribute: Parameter includeEmpty True to also note locations with no region, for adding and removing regions.
    */
    private action CopyRegionsFor(integer minimumX, integer minimumZ, integer maximumX, integer maximumZ, boolean includeEmpty)
        integer firstLocationX = data:GetRegionLocation(minimumX)
        integer lastLocationX = data:GetRegionLocation(maximumX)
        integer firstLocationZ = data:GetRegionLocation(minimumZ)
        integer lastLocationZ = data:GetRegionLocation(maximumZ)
        integer locationZ = firstLocationZ
        repeat while locationZ <= lastLocationZ
            integer locationX = firstLocationX
            repeat while locationX <= lastLocationX
                CopyRegion(locationX, locationZ, includeEmpty)
                locationX = locationX + 1
            end
            locationZ = locationZ + 1
        end
    end

    /*
    This action keeps a copy of the region at a location, if the stroke
    hasn't touched it yet.

    Attribute: Parameter locationX The region location along x.
    Attribute: Parameter locationZ The region location along z.
    Attribute: Parameter includeEmpty True to note the location even if there is no region there.
    */
    private action CopyRegion(integer locationX, integer locationZ, boolean includeEmpty)
        integer i = 0
        repeat while i < touchedX:GetSize()
            if touchedX:Get(i) = locationX and touchedZ:Get(i) = locationZ
                return now
            end
            i = i + 1
        end
        TerrainRegion region = data:GetRegion(locationX, locationZ)
        if region = undefined
            if includeEmpty and data:IsInRegionMap(locationX, locationZ)
                touchedX:Add(locationX)
                touchedZ:Add(locationZ)
                beforeCopies:Add(undefined)
            end
            return now
        end
        touchedX:Add(locationX)
        touchedZ:Add(locationZ)
        beforeCopies:Add(region:Copy())
    end

    /*
    This action returns how far a value moves toward its goal: 1 minus e to
    the power of minus strength times seconds times weight. Applying it
    twice for half the time moves exactly as far as once for the whole time,
    which is what makes a stroke the same at any frame rate.

    Attribute: Parameter weight The brush's weight at the sample.
    Attribute: Parameter seconds How long the brush is held.
    Attribute: Returns The fraction of the way to move, from 0 to just under 1.
    */
    private action GetFraction(number weight, number seconds) returns number
        number exponent = brush:GetStrength() * seconds * weight
        if exponent <= 0
            return 0
        end
        return 1 - math:RaiseNaturalNumberToPower(-exponent)
    end

    /*
    This action returns how far around a sample smoothing and blending look,
    in samples: a quarter of the brush's size, from 1 to 3. A wider brush
    smooths broader shapes; 1 means the sample and its eight neighbors.

    Attribute: Returns The radius in samples.
    */
    private action GetAverageRadius returns integer
        number samples = brush:GetSize() / data:GetVertexSpacing() / 4
        return cast(integer, math:Clamp(math:Round(samples), 1, 3))
    end

    /*
    This action returns the average height of the samples with regions in
    the square around a sample, GetAverageRadius samples each way.

    Attribute: Parameter x The sample along x.
    Attribute: Parameter z The sample along z.
    Attribute: Returns The average height.
    */
    private action GetAverageHeight(integer x, integer z) returns number
        integer radius = GetAverageRadius()
        number total = 0
        integer count = 0
        integer offsetZ = -radius
        repeat while offsetZ <= radius
            integer offsetX = -radius
            repeat while offsetX <= radius
                if data:HasSample(x + offsetX, z + offsetZ)
                    total = total + data:GetSampleHeight(x + offsetX, z + offsetZ)
                    count = count + 1
                end
                offsetX = offsetX + 1
            end
            offsetZ = offsetZ + 1
        end
        if count = 0
            return data:GetSampleHeight(x, z)
        end
        return total / count
    end

    /*
    This action writes the average splat weights of the samples with regions
    in the square around a sample, GetAverageRadius samples each way, into
    four places of an array: red, green, blue and alpha.

    Attribute: Parameter x The sample along x.
    Attribute: Parameter z The sample along z.
    Attribute: Parameter goals The array to write into.
    Attribute: Parameter start Where in the array the four weights go.
    */
    private action FillAverageSplat(integer x, integer z, Number32BitArray goals, integer start)
        number red = 0
        number green = 0
        number blue = 0
        number alpha = 0
        integer count = 0
        integer radius = GetAverageRadius()
        integer offsetZ = -radius
        repeat while offsetZ <= radius
            integer offsetX = -radius
            repeat while offsetX <= radius
                if data:HasSample(x + offsetX, z + offsetZ)
                    integer code = data:GetSampleSplat(x + offsetX, z + offsetZ)
                    red = red + data:GetSplatWeight(code, 0)
                    green = green + data:GetSplatWeight(code, 1)
                    blue = blue + data:GetSplatWeight(code, 2)
                    alpha = alpha + data:GetSplatWeight(code, 3)
                    count = count + 1
                end
                offsetX = offsetX + 1
            end
            offsetZ = offsetZ + 1
        end
        if count = 0
            count = 1
        end
        goals:Set(start, red / count)
        goals:Set(start + 1, green / count)
        goals:Set(start + 2, blue / count)
        goals:Set(start + 3, alpha / count)
    end

    /*
    This action moves a splat weight part of the way toward a goal. Weights
    are stored as whole steps of 1/255, so a small move could round back to
    where it started, and a slow brush at a high frame rate would never
    change anything. So if the move rounds to no change while the goal is a
    different step, the weight moves one whole step toward it instead.

    Attribute: Parameter weight The weight now, from 0 to 1.
    Attribute: Parameter goal The weight to move toward, from 0 to 1.
    Attribute: Parameter fraction How far to move, from 0 to 1.
    Attribute: Returns The new weight.
    */
    private action MoveWeight(number weight, number goal, number fraction) returns number
        if fraction <= 0
            return weight
        end
        number moved = weight + (goal - weight) * fraction
        number step = 1 / 255.0
        number start = math:Round(weight * 255)
        number target = math:Round(goal * 255)
        if math:Round(moved * 255) = start and target not= start
            if target > start
                return (start + 1) * step
            else
                return (start - 1) * step
            end
        end
        return moved
    end
end
